"Board Exam Question: What is the maximum value that can be stored in DECIMAL(3,2)? Total digits (p) = 3, digits after decimal (s) = 2. Digits before decimal = p - s = 3 - 2 = 1. Therefore, maximum value is 9.99! If a movie gets rating 10.0, it will cause an 'Out of range value' error!"
